# Files in THIS directory that must not be uploaded to HCP Terraform.
#
# Background: this workspace uses HCP for remote execution, and CLI-driven runs
# package up the working directory — including subdirectories — and ship it to
# HCP as a configuration version.
#
# `keycloak/` is a SEPARATE, LOCALLY-executed root module (ADR-0015). Terraform
# never evaluates it as part of this root module (it is not referenced as a
# module), so uploading it would change nothing — but it holds a LOCAL
# terraform.tfstate containing secrets, and there is no reason to hand that to a
# remote service. Excluded explicitly rather than trusting the default ignore
# rules, which are not clearly documented on this point.
keycloak/
